  "query_preview": "(Saturday through Tuesday)...\nA weak trough of low pressure moving inland into northern and\ncentral California on Sunday and Monday could bring slight cooling\nfor coastal areas for Sunday through Tuesday followed by weaker\nonshore flow near the coast returning by Wednesday.\n\nECMWF ensemble output for Campo is strongest with the offshore \nwinds on Saturday with uncalibrated gusts to around 40 mph. High\ntemperatures on Saturday could be another 5 or so degrees warmer\nfor coastal areas into the western valleys with high temperatures\nranging from around 90 near the coast to the upper 90s to 108 for\nthe valleys with the lower deserts around 100. Low temperatures \non Saturday will be mostly in the lower 70s for coastal areas, \naround 10 degrees above average. Widespread Major HeatRisk is \nexpected for the coast and valleys on Saturday. \n\nFor Sunday through Tuesday, low temperatures for the coast into\nthe western valleys will warm into the lower to mid 70s, 10 to 15\ndegrees above average. Moderate HeatRisk will continue for the far\ninland valleys with Major to Extreme HeatRisk for inland coastal\nareas into the western valleys. \n\nThis long-dursation heat wave, with highest HeatRisk for the \ncoast and valleys, may continue through much of next week into \nthe following weekend.",
